        <div class="card-sub">Unit 1 · Building a Classroom Community</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="def-box">
      <div class="label">📌 Definição</div>
      <p>Irregular verbs are verbs that do <strong>NOT</strong> follow the regular rule when changed to the past. Regular verbs simply add <strong>-ed</strong>; irregular verbs change in their own unique way.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pt-tip">🇧🇷 Em português: verbos irregulares mudam de forma diferente no passado, assim como em inglês — eles simplesmente precisam ser memorizados!</div>

    <div class="compare-grid">
      <div class="compare-card a">
        <strong>✅ Regular Verbs (add -ed)</strong>
        <span>play → <b>played</b><br>walk → <b>walked</b><br>jump → <b>jumped</b></span>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-card b">
        <strong>⚡ Irregular Verbs (own rule)</strong>
        <span>go → <b>went</b><br>eat → <b>ate</b><br>see → <b>saw</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="memory-box">
      <div class="emoji">🧠</div>
      <div>
        <strong>Dica de Memória</strong>
        <p>Alguns verbos irregulares são "unchanging" — ficam iguais nas 3 formas: <b>cut→cut→cut</b>, <b>put→put→put</b>, <b>cost→cost→cost</b>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Base Form</th><th>Simple Past</th><th>Past Participle</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
