  <!-- ELA_2 · Past Perfect -->
  <div class="card" id="ela2">
    <div class="card-header">
      <div class="card-icon green">⏪</div>
      <div>
        <div class="card-title">ELA 2 · Past Perfect</div>
        <div class="card-sub">Unit 1 · Building a Classroom Community</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="def-box">
      <div class="label">📌 Definição</div>
      <p>We use <strong>HAD + past participle</strong> to talk about something that happened <strong>BEFORE</strong> another action in the past. This is called Past Perfect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="formula">Subject + <b>HAD</b> + past participle</div>

    <div class="pt-tip">🇧🇷 Em português equivale ao <b>Pretérito Mais-que-perfeito</b>: "Eu <u>já tinha comido</u> quando ela chegou."</div>

    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="tl-node">HAD + participle</div>
      <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="tl-node">Simple Past</div>
      <div class="tl-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="tl-node">NOW</div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:#64748b;font-weight:600;margin:.3rem 0 .8rem;">A ação com HAD acontece PRIMEIRO. A ação no simple past acontece DEPOIS.</p>

    <div class="memory-box">
      <div class="emoji">💡</div>
      <div>
        <strong>Como Lembrar</strong>
        <p>Pense em uma linha do tempo: <b>Past Perfect (HAD)</b> fica ANTES do <b>Simple Past</b>. O que veio primeiro usa HAD!</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="examples">
      <li>I <b>had eaten</b> before I went to school. <span class="ex-tr">(comi primeiro, depois fui)</span></li>
      <li>She <b>had finished</b> her homework before dinner. <span class="ex-tr">(ela terminou antes do jantar)</span></li>
      <li>We <b>had studied</b> all night before the exam. <span class="ex-tr">(estudamos antes da prova)</span></li>
      <li>He <b>had gone</b> home before it rained. <span class="ex-tr">(foi para casa antes de chover)</span></li>
      <li>By the time the teacher arrived, students <b>had finished</b> the test.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="quiz-section">
      <h3>🎯 Quiz — Past Perfect</h3>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="b">
        <p>1. What structure is used for <b>Past Perfect</b>?</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) have + past participle</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) had + past participle</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) was + verb + ing</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) will + verb</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ Past Perfect = <b>HAD + past participle</b>!</div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="b">
        <p>2. Choose the correct <b>Past Perfect</b> sentence:</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) She has eaten before he arrived.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) She had eaten before he arrived.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) She have eaten before he arrived.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) She eating before he arrived.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ <b>had eaten</b> — Past Perfect correto!</div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="b">
        <p>3. In "He <b>had gone</b> home before it rained", which action happened <b>FIRST</b>?</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) It rained</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) He went home</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) Both at the same time</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) None of the above</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ <b>He had gone home</b> — o Past Perfect indica a ação que veio PRIMEIRO!</div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="c">
        <p>4. What is the <b>past participle</b> of "study"?</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) studyed</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) studying</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) studied</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) studyied</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ study → <b>studied</b> (regular verb: -y vira -ied)!</div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="a">
        <p>5. Complete: "By the time she arrived, I _____ (finish) the homework."</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) had finished</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) finished</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) have finished</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) was finishing</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ <b>had finished</b> — aconteceu ANTES dela chegar, então usa Past Perfect!</div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-q" data-correct="c">
        <p>6. Which sentence is <b>NOT</b> in Past Perfect?</p>
        <div class="quiz-opts">
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="a">a) She had read the book before the test.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="b">b) They had left when I arrived.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="c">c) He was eating dinner.</div>
          <div class="quiz-opt" data-opt="d">d) We had studied before the exam.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-fb">✅ <b>"He was eating"</b> é Past Continuous, não Past Perfect!</div>
      </div>
    </div>

