      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="def-box">
      <div class="label">📌 Definição</div>
      <p>Adverbs of manner tell us <strong>HOW</strong> an action happens. They usually come <strong>AFTER the verb</strong>. Most are formed by adding <strong>-LY</strong> to an adjective.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="formula">Adjective + <b>-ly</b> = Adverb of Manner</div>

    <div class="pt-tip">🇧🇷 Em português, muitas vezes equivale a palavras que terminam em <b>-mente</b>: quickly = <b>rapidamente</b>, softly = <b>suavemente</b>.</div>

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Regra</th><th>Exemplo</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Most: add -ly</td><td>quick → <b>quickly</b>, soft → <b>softly</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ends in -y: → -ily</td><td>happy → <b>happily</b>, easy → <b>easily</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ends in -le: → -ly</td><td>gentle → <b>gently</b>, simple → <b>simply</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td>⚠️ good → well (irregular)</td><td>She sings <b>well</b>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>⚠️ fast → fast (no change)</td><td>He runs <b>fast</b>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>⚠️ hard → hard (no change)</td><td>She works <b>hard</b>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <ul class="examples">
      <li>He runs <b>quickly</b>. <span class="ex-tr">(quick → quickly)</span></li>
      <li>She speaks <b>softly</b>. <span class="ex-tr">(soft → softly)</span></li>
      <li>They walk <b>slowly</b>. <span class="ex-tr">(slow → slowly)</span></li>
      <li>He works <b>carefully</b>. <span class="ex-tr">(careful → carefully)</span></li>
      <li>She sings <b>beautifully</b>. <span class="ex-tr">(beautiful → beautifully)</span></li>
      <li>Fudge runs <b>wildly</b> through the apartment. <span class="ex-tr">(from the book!)</span></li>
      <li>Peter speaks <b>quietly</b> to his parents. <span class="ex-tr">(from the book!)</span></li>
    </ul>

